>Hello all...
>	How does one obtain named weapons?  I know
>how to get Excalibur, and usually obtain it, but how 
>does one get the others which you can't get from
>a fountain.

Well, there are several ways to do it:
1)  Well, a wish is always the easiest.  Ask for a +3 weapon, not +99 or
something like that.
2)  Be a luck stiff like me and find them in shops or on ghost stacks.(sorry
Paul, but you called this one a bit off.  I was smashed by a demon using
Mjollnir from MY OWN GHOST STACK!!!) Heck, I once got Stormbringer for 26 gp
in a shop, and I found fire brand on a goblin!
3)  Keep sacrificing to your god, eventually an object will appear at your
feet.  It will be a sword of like alignment.

>	Also, how do you change alignment?  I don't
>know how to identify aligned or unaligned altars.

The key is to use the ':' command.  It will tell you what altar you are
standing on.  My favorite way to change alignment(usually to Lawful) is to
kill my pet and sacrifice it.  Killing it will make my deity mad, and the
other deity will accept me if I sacrifice it on his altar.  You can also use a
help of opposite alignment, and sacrifice at any altar you want, just keep
re-wearing the helm until you are the correct alignment.

